# BuildKit picks this up instead of .dockerignore when building with -f Dockerfile.builder64.
# Same reason as Dockerfile.builder.dockerignore: the builder image BAKES IN the prebuilt
# cross-compiled dep tree, so unlike the main Dockerfile (which gets deps from this image and
# must exclude them) deps/ MUST be in this context. Without this file the main .dockerignore
# excludes `deps` and the COPY fails.
#
# Differs from the wasm32 one in exactly one way: this image needs deps/wasm64 and NOT
# deps/wasm. Shipping the wasm32 stack here would add ~600 MB of archives that can never be
# linked into this image's builds -- wasm-ld refuses to mix the two models.
.git
.github
openmw/.git-upstream
archive
source-mw
content
node_modules
infra
build-wasm
build-wasm32
build-wasm64
build-wasm.good
build-native
build-bullet-native
build-mygui-native
build-memory64-gate
deps/native
deps/wasm
.wasm32-backup
.logs
wasm-build/mod-src
play/mwdata
play/moddata
